## Graph inventory and planned executable mapping

Both graphs: one shared coordinate plane, 25 lattice bands per direction,
24 strips per direction; origin column2/row22, x=.5 column12, x=1 column22,
y=10 row2; ordinary dx=.05, dy=.5. Two full left/top margin strips, one
full right/bottom strip beyond x=1/y=0, then a shorter terminal strip.
English x/y/O, x ticks .5/1, y ticks 1..10, positive axis arrows.
Captions remain outside the media and are not newly drawn in the spec.

Mapping:
- lattice-full: 23x23 grid, bounds [-.1,11,1.05,-.5], gridDimensions.
- lattice-right: 1x23 partial grid, gridDimensions.
- lattice-bottom: 23x1 partial grid, gridDimensions.
- lattice-corner: 1x1 partial grid, gridDimensions.
- frame/axis tick anchors: literal displacement assertions bind origin/tick
  positions to the full-grid corner and unit scale; axis/arrow connects.
- source y label, x label, O, and each tick get stable source-derived IDs.

MODERN CHOICE, NOT SOURCE FRACTIONS: terminal right width .025 (half a full
dx step), terminal bottom height .3 (three-fifths a full dy step).
These preserve visibly short strips and topology without claiming to recover
their exact scan fractions. All full strips are made straight/equal; scan skew
is deliberately removed. Pixel axis arrow footprints and dash gaps are not
recovered. Renderer-owned arrowheads/dash pattern are modern choices.
The mathematical unit ratio is 10:1: one x unit spans ten times one y unit;
the added English unit legend makes x=10 cm / y=1 cm explicit. Physical CSS
pixels are not a claim of literal ruler centimetres.

fig-81: exactly nine filled, unnamed dots:
(0,1.00),(.125,1.33),(.25,1.78),(.375,2.37),(.5,3.16),
(.625,4.22),(.75,5.63),(.875,7.50),(1,10.00).
Map sample-00..08 and consecutive displacement assertions; all nine points
are covered inside the inventory group requiring pointRelationships.
No curve, no curve label, no guide, no added point.
Source dot pixel centres are not substituted for authoritative rounded pairs.

fig-82: one solid increasing convex curve from (0,1) to (1,10), no extension,
no curve arrow, no visible point markers; interior label y=10^x.
Map exponential-curve and three pairs of dashed read-off segments.
The first two source prose examples .37 -> approximately2.3 and
.82 -> approximately6.6 are NOT exact equalities.
MODERN CHOICE: sample the stated function y=10^x on [0,1] and use the
existing svgPath object with tangent-based cubic pieces. This is mathematical
regularization, NOT restoration of original scan control points. Guide endpoints
use this mathematical curve at the prose x values, while the source approximate
y readings remain explicitly approximate. No read-off labels are added.
Each guide has connects plus horizontal/vertical displacement assertions.
There are no visible source point objects in fig-82; pointRelationships is not
faked by adding markers. Literal endpoint/guide and table-pair assertions are
mapped instead. Additional curve construction checks are author evidence, not
an independent source-fidelity verdict.

## Table inventory and planned executable mapping

All: two rows, six logical columns; three horizontal rules, five interior
separators; open outer vertical sides. x and 10^x source row labels become
English mathematical x and y=10^x, with the y addition declared.

217 x: 0; 1/8(0.125); 1/4(0.250); 3/8(0.375); 1/2(0.500).
217 y: 1.00; 1.33; 1.78; 2.37; 3.16.
218 x: 5/8(0.625); 3/4(0.750); 7/8(0.875); 1; blank.
218 y: 4.22; 5.63; 7.50; 10.00; blank.
219 x: 7/16(0.438); 9/16(0.563); 11/16(0.688);
13/16(0.813); 15/16(0.938).
219 y: 2.74; 3.65; 4.86; 6.49; 8.65.
217+218 partition nine first-table pairs, never repeat the first five in218.
219 is a separate five-pair refinement table.

The existing grid renderer always draws boundary lines. Preserve open sides
with one visible interior grid (four interior cell intervals, two rows) plus
the two open edge columns' extended horizontal rules. gridDimensions covers
the real 4x2 interior grid; literal displacement assertions each cover the
one-cell left/right margins, giving 1+4+1=6 logical columns and2 rows.
Do not falsely assert the interior grid itself has six columns, add outer
vertical borders, or use objectCount in place of these dimensions.
Each source cell maps to its text/fraction-bar IDs and coordinate/pair assertions.
Fractions use renderer-owned numerator/denominator text and segment bars;
parenthesized decimals remain paired and unchanged. Modern spacing/font/rule
weight and uniform column widths are not source-pixel facts.

